  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d29a6973-3146-4a73-9c9a-ce7907591d03",
      "type": "Output/Note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -420,
      "w": 620,
      "h": 250,
      "state": {
        "Text": "12 \u2014 WATCHING A LOG   (run it continuously: Ctrl\u002BShift\u002BR)\n\nEvery few seconds the graph appends a line to %TEMP%\\vnoder-sample-12.log, and File Tail reads back only the lines added since the last pass, the way tail -f does. Run Once just steps it.\n\n\u2022 Every slows one branch down: true once per interval, however fast the run ticks.\n\u2022 File Tail remembers where it stopped, holds back a half-written line, and starts again if the file is rotated.\n\u2022 Switch maps the level to what to do, with wildcards and a default.\n\u2022 Cron Due is true on the tick where a schedule comes round (here, every minute); Next says when that is."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "168a1afa-7c19-43d8-898a-58e1fac9af3c",
